        <mxCell id="audit_events_c6" value="    append-only, 180-day retention" style="text;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=10;overflow=hidden;html=1;fontSize=12;fontFamily=Courier New;" vertex="1" parent="audit_events">
          <mxGeometry y="216" width="340" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="legend" value="Reading this diagram

• showtime_seats is the only current seat-allocation authority. hold_id and booking_id name the CURRENT owner: confirmation clears hold_id, blocking clears both (RC-02).
• History is never read from a live pointer — hold_items, booking_items, bookings.hold_id and audit_events preserve it.
• Every requested seat locks in seat_id order behind the showtime lock; a hold is all-or-none.
• payment_callback_events deduplicates on (provider, provider_event_id); a callback is recorded even when it cannot change the payment.
• cancellations covers customer, admin and showtime cancellation in one idempotent decision record (RC-06).
• Not drawn, to keep the graph legible: users ← cancellations.requested_by_user_id and users ← audit_events.actor_user_id, both ON DELETE SET NULL.
• Laravel jobs / failed_jobs are infrastructure tables and are out of the logical model." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;fontSize=12;dashed=1;rounded=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
